PrismNet - an open-source TCP/IP stack for AmigaOS 3.x
======================================================

PrismNet gives your Amiga networking through any SANA-II network driver
(PCMCIA cards like cnet.device, X-Surf, ZZ9000, DaynaPORT, A314, serial
SLIP/PPP). Programs written for AmiTCP, Miami or Roadshow - web browsers,
wget, FTP, IRC, mail - work unchanged: PrismNet provides the same
bsdsocket.library they expect.

It is free and open source (GNU GPL version 3). The networking core is lwIP.

The full manual is PrismNet.guide in this drawer: double-click it.

Requirements
------------
- AmigaOS 3.0 or newer, any 68000 or better
- a SANA-II driver for your network hardware in DEVS:Networks
- about 290 KB of free memory while running (175 KB with the small core
  for 1-2 MB machines; the installer offers it)

Installing
----------
Double-click "Install_PrismNet". It installs the libraries, the PrismNet
command, PrismNet Prefs, the PrismMon monitor and this manual, and asks
for your network driver and DHCP or a fixed address. Another stack's
libraries are saved in C:Backup. Optional: network-share clients (NFS,
SMB) and servers (FTP, telnet).

Run it again to update (your settings are kept) or to remove PrismNet.

Using it
--------
Usually there is nothing to do: the first program that wants the network
starts PrismNet. In a Shell:

  PrismNet START      start in the background and show the status
  PrismNet STATUS     interfaces, addresses, DNS, memory
  PrismNet STOP
  PrismNet NETSTAT    open connections
  PrismNet ROUTE      the routes
  PrismNet ARP        hardware addresses on the LAN
  PrismNet LOG        recent messages

PrismNet Prefs (SYS:Prefs/PrismNet) changes every setting; PrismMon shows
what the stack is doing. Settings live in plain text files in
ENVARC:PrismNet (commented examples in ENVARC:PrismNet/examples).

Problems
--------
See "Troubleshooting" in the manual. Please report problems with the
output of "PrismNet STATUS" and "PrismNet LOG".

